Actually, both your character's XP level and the current dungeon level
influence monster generation. The deepest dungeon level visited doest
not play a role at all unless you are carrying the Amulet of Yendor or
are in the Endgame.

These two numbers influence both what monster species become eligible
to be created randomly, and also they adjust the experience level
monsters get, including those created by other, more specific
mechanisms.

Starting with dungeon level 14, dragons become eligible for throne
room population (and throne looting). You also have to go quite deep
to meet dragons created by random generation or special levels.

However, you can have dragons on dungeon level 1 by reverse genocide.
In my experience, dragons are always generated at monster experience
level 14 on dungeon level 1. I myself was also quite low-level in
those cases, else I wouldn't have bothered trecking back up.

See the source for the full details how monster levels are adjusted. I
am not aware of a good spoiler on this subject.
